    "updated_at": "2021-09-23T09:30:44Z",
    "body": "Thinking about this and also about https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/issues/590, I think that we need something like a \"fetch a resource\" algorithm/layer/mechanism in the HTML spec, equivalent to the different resource loaders found in the browser engine implementation. \r\n\r\nThis mechanism would deal with setting the initiator type for the resource when reporting, reporting network errors as opaque entries, setting FETCH priority by type, and keeping the `preload` responses.\r\n\r\n@annevk WDYT? I can start jotting down something.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/925648073/reactions",
