    "body": "> I see, generally I would like network error reporting to fall out of the same path we use for normal reporting and not require its own dedicated path.\r\n\r\nIt generally wouldn't, except when the caller already has a dedicated path for network errors (like in the case of `fetch()` and `xhr`. We'll get to that when we start implementing these calls. I assume most of them will share a single call that fully loads an URL and reports at the end.",
